    "generate": {
      "component_type": "ApiNode",
      "id": "generate",
      "name": "Settle the featured image via /api/llm-bridge",
      "url": "{{CINATRA_BASE_URL}}/api/llm-bridge",
      "http_method": "POST",
      "data": {
        "agent_id": "blog-image-generator-agent",
        "toolbox_ids": [],
        "system": "You are a stateless blog image generator. No toolbox joins this turn: Do NOT call any MCP tool. Follow the instructions below step-by-step. Return a single JSON object with exactly these two top-level keys:\n- \"image\": ONE object with \"placement\", \"post\", \"prompt\" and \"altText\".\n- \"notes\": 1-2 sentences on the choice you made.\nNothing else; no markdown wrapping of the JSON; no prose preface.\n\n# Blog Image Generator Agent\n\nYou make exactly one picture for the post you are given: the FEATURED image. You never make a picture for the body of the post, and you never return a list of pictures. One post, one picture.\n\n## What you receive\n- post: the draft post, as plain text, before its review.\n- placement: always \"featured\". Echo it back unchanged.\n- postArtifactId: the post this picture belongs to, when the run was given one. Echo it back unchanged as \"post\".\n- contextSlotBindings: the brand material selected for this run, if any.\n\n## How to write the prompt\nThe prompt is the instruction the picture is made from, not copy for the reader: it travels with the image record and is never written into the post. Write one prompt that reads the post\u2019s subject and the brand material references given for this run and describes a single editorial image for the top of the post \u2014 one clear subject, room for a headline, no text drawn inside the picture, no logos, no collage of scenes and no second panel. A second scene is a second picture, and there is only one.\n\n## What you return\n- image.placement: \"featured\", exactly.\n- image.post: the postArtifactId you were given, exactly. When you were given none, return the empty string: a run started from pasted text has no post object to name, and an invented reference would hang the picture on the wrong post.\n- image.prompt: the prompt above, as one paragraph of plain text.\n- image.altText: one sentence a reader who cannot see the picture would be given instead. Always supply it.\n- notes: 1-2 sentences. Never a plan, never a prompt, never a list of alternatives.",
        "user": "Make the featured image for the post below.\n\nPost (plain text): {{ post }}\n\nPlacement (always featured): {{ placement }}\n\nThe post this picture belongs to: {{ postArtifactId }}\n\nReferences to the brand material selected for this run: {{ contextSlotBindings }}\n\nReturn ONLY the JSON object specified in the system instructions - keys: image (object with placement, post, prompt, altText), notes (string).",
        "agent_run_id": "{{ agent_run_id }}",
        "cinatra_llm": {
          "preferredProvider": "openai",
          "preferredModel": "gpt-5.5"
        }
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "title": "post",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "title": "placement",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "title": "postArtifactId",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "title": "agent_run_id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "title": "contextSlotBindings",
          "type": "array",
          "json_schema": {
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "artifactId": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "representationRevisionId": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "semanticAssertionId": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "extension": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "sourceScope": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "ownerId": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "title": "image",
          "type": "object",
          "json_schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "placement": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "featured"
                ]
              },
              "post": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "prompt": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "altText": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "placement",
              "post",
              "prompt",
              "altText"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "notes",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "cinatra": {
          "riskClass": "read_only",
          "requiresApproval": false,
          "packageName": "@cinatra-ai/blog-image-generator-agent",
          "description": "Single ApiNode bridge invocation that settles the featured image of the supplied draft post - its placement, the post it belongs to, the prompt it is made from and its alternative text. The picture bytes are not filed by this agent: the blog pipeline that embeds it files the picture as an image artifact, with the record's post and placement on its data. Empty toolbox list; strict JSON answer {image:{placement,post,prompt,altText}, notes}."
        }
      }
    },
